    "lawCode": "Add §29-e, Veterans' Services L",
    "lawSection": "Veterans' Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S274A\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the veterans' services law, in relation to establishing\nthe \"Vets to Vollies\" program\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nEstablishes the \"Vets to Vollies\" program.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\n1 Section 1. The veterans' services law is amended by adding a new\nsection 29-b to read as follows: § 29-e. Vets to vollies. 1. The depart-\nment shall create a statewide \"Vets to Vollies\" program for counties\nthat wish to participate in such program. The purpose of such program is\nto encourage veterans or discharged military personnel to join their\nlocal fire department or emergency medical service agency. 2. Such\nprogram shall collaborate and coordinate with all applicable county\nagencies to conduct extensive outreach programs within the local commu-\nnity, including but not limited to, active military installations and\nlocal veteran service organizations. Such outreach programs shall\nprovide information on the many benefits and resources available to\nprospective volunteer first responders on a local and statewide level\nand how to further become involved.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis legislation will establish a statewide program where veterans or\ndischarged military personnel are encouraged to volunteer (\"Vets to\nVollies\") in their local fire department or EMS agency. The Vets To\nVollies program offers our military heroes an opportunity to serve their\ncommunity utilizing similar skills and job duties performed while in\nservice, provides them with a sense of purpose and belonging, as well as\nassists first responder agencies in recruiting new members. It is a\nvital measure that would benefit our veteran community greatly.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA.8125\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nNone.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
