    "lawCode": "Amd §§4 & 15, Veterans' Services L",
    "lawSection": "Veterans' Service Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S274B\n\nSPONSOR: MARTINEZ\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the veterans' services law, in relation to establishing\nvoluntary opportunities for veterans\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to increase awareness of volunteer opportu-\nnities available to veterans. SUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill requires the Department of Veteran Services to\nprovide information on the department's we bsite on volunteer opportu-\nnities available to veterans and post any relevant application forms on\nthe employment portal.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides those local veterans' service agencies\nhave an obligation to inform members of the uniformed services and their\nfamilies of any volunteer opportunities at the department.\n\nSection three provides the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nMany times veterans when they come back home want to continue to serve\ntheir community but they may not know how to start the process. This\nbill requires the Department of Veterans' Services to provide on their\nwe bsite information about volunteering at a volunteer fire department\nor emergency services provider. Many voluntary fire departments and\nemergency services across the state are looking to increase the number\nof volunteers and this bill would tap into ready available qualified\ncandidates.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect on the ninetieth day after it shall have\nbecome a law. Effective immediately, the addition, amendment and/or\nrepeal of any rule or regulation necessary forthe implementation of this\nact on its effective date are authorized to be made and completed on or\nbefore such date.\n",
